   [
    "Summary",
    "<ul>\n<li>Part 2 (War), in 1450: 6 chapters per route, with no Free Time or shops. It is the same campaign for all four lords, with scenes of their own.</li>\n<li>Before each battle, the Dispatch Officer offers one Army Action out of three and hands out weapons and licenses.</li>\n<li>Units enter raised to level 35. Skipping the War shows a summary and adds 5 levels, but does not give its 120 Karma Shards; you can still play it later.</li>\n<li>Clearing or skipping it saves that route's copy of the army, which carries over to <a href=\"#/guia/parte-3-salvacion\">Part 3</a>; without that, its units do not appear.</li>\n</ul>"
   ],
   [
    "On entering",
    "<p>Clearing ch. 12 leads straight into that lord's War. Only the weapons and equipment each character is carrying go in; Part 1's Storage, mounts and battalions stay stored. <a href=\"#/objeto/IID_開かれし救世の剣\">Chosen Sword</a>, <a href=\"#/objeto/IID_氷の救世の槍\">Chosen Lance</a>, <a href=\"#/objeto/IID_ブレイザブリク\">Breidablik</a> and <a href=\"#/objeto/IID_王家の宝剣\">Royal Sword</a> cannot be taken, but Part 2 gives you their +1 versions.</p>"
   ],
   [
    "Dispatch Officer",
    "<p>«Main Quest» ends the preparations and starts the battle (<a href=\"#/tutorial/TUTO_行軍管理官\">tutorial</a>). «Army Action» lets you pick one of three per chapter:</p>\n<div class=\"tw\"><table class=\"md\"><tr><th>Action</th><th>Effect</th></tr><tr><td>Training Drills</td><td>Trains the lowest-level units to bring them closer to the strongest</td></tr><tr><td>Group Drills</td><td>Raises the whole group's skills</td></tr><tr><td>Group Service</td><td>Everyone serves a deity to raise the tribute</td></tr></table></div>\n<p><b>Supplies.</b> Each chapter hands out +3 iron and bronze weapons of each type, +2 throwing weapons, <a href=\"#/objeto/IID_調合薬\">Concoction</a>, <a href=\"#/objeto/IID_毒消し\">Antitoxin</a> and 5 licenses of each level. Depending on the route, ingredients (Cai), 100 <a href=\"#/objeto/IID_魔響石\">Magic Echo Shards</a> (Dietrich) or plants (Leda) also arrive. These +3 weapons do not carry over to Part 3.</p>\n<p><b>Slots.</b> Not counting the lord, you pick 8 units in ch. 1 and 12 in the others (on Theodora's route, 9, 13, 13, 12, 13 and 13). Preparations have no deadline.</p>"
   ],
   [
    "When it ends",
    "<ul>\n<li><a href=\"#/objeto/IID_妖槍ヴェンデッタ\">Vendetta</a>, <a href=\"#/objeto/IID_邪剣エンジュラ\">Angela</a> and <a href=\"#/objeto/IID_ダグザの棍棒\">Dagda's Club</a> are taken away; the Club goes to whoever defeats Dagda's first form in ch. 5.</li>\n<li>Replaying a War replaces that route's previous copy.</li>\n<li><b>Drifting Reliquary.</b> When Part 2 closes, Part 1's items, materials, mounts and battalions go into the Drifting Reliquary in the Obelisk Chamber; replaying a War that was already closed does not fill it again. In Part 3 you take them out in exchange for <a href=\"#/guia/esquirlas\">Karma Shards</a>: mounts need Cai in the army and battalions need Theodora, both joined fully.</li>\n<li><b>Lords' bags.</b> When each lord joins in Part 3, the game hands over for free what their Storage and their materials bag held, once per lord; whatever doesn't fit is lost. It arrives after section 1<span class=\"gu-com\" title=\"Community fact\"><span class=\"sr-only\">(community fact)</span></span>.</li>\n<li>Gold does not go into the Reliquary: each path keeps its own. Renown gives way to Relief Lv.</li>\n</ul>"
   ],
   [
    "Skipping it",
    "<p>«Skip the War Arc» shows a summary and allies improve on their own (+5 levels); you can also skip halfway, losing what you played. It counts as cleared for Part 3, saves the units and goes through the same closing step that fills the Reliquary. What you lose: the 120 shards and the scenes that need a War played in full (Fortuna's promise, and another that also needs Dietrich or Theodora). Theodora has scenes of her own in Part 3 if her War was played.</p>"
   ],
   [
    "Min-max tips",
    "<ul>\n<li>Play at least one War in full (scenes and 120 shards) and skip the others if you don't need their trained copy.</li>\n<li>Before clearing or skipping each Part 2, train high-growth units by hand and load them with the best gear: that is the copy that carries over.</li>\n<li>Close all four lords' Part 2 to have them fully in Part 3.</li>\n<li>«Training Drills» to even out levels and «Group Service» if you are short on blessings.</li>\n<li>In Part 3, make room in Storage before each lord joins: whatever doesn't fit from their bag is lost.</li>\n</ul>"
   ]
